course: dictionary
lesson: 13588
title: Words that do not fit together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Incompatible means not able to work together or exist together. Look at the sentence around it for clues. «My new game is incompatible with my old console, so it will not load.» The game will not load, so the two things cannot work together.
explain: People can be incompatible too. «The two flatmates were incompatible: one loved loud music and the other needed quiet to study.» Their habits clash, so they are too different to live well together. Always ask: what would fit here? Try the meaning "not able to work together" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Ideas can be incompatible as well. «Her story says the door was locked, but it also says she walked straight through it, so the two claims are incompatible.» If both cannot be true at once, they are incompatible.
fact: Incompatible means not able to work together or exist together.
fact: «Compatible» means able to work together well. The prefix in- means not, so «incompatible» means not compatible.
fact: «Incompatible» can describe devices, apps, people, ideas, and blood types.
fact: In medicine, «incompatible» blood types cannot be safely mixed in a transfusion, so doctors test blood first.
fact: Useful phrases: «incompatible with» and «completely incompatible».
exercise: «My new game is incompatible with my old console, so it will not load.» What does incompatible mean here? | Brand new and shiny | Easy to play with friends | *Not able to work together | Very fast and powerful
exercise: «Doctors test blood before a transfusion, because some blood types are incompatible.» Why do doctors test the blood? | *Some blood types cannot be safely mixed | To check the patient is tall | To make the blood colder
exercise: Which word in this sentence means not able to get along? «Mia and Sam were incompatible flatmates, so they moved apart.» | flatmates | apart | *incompatible | moved
test: «The two ideas were incompatible, because both could not be true at once.» What does incompatible mean? | Very large | Both could be true | Easy to understand | *Cannot both be true at once
test: Ben says incompatible means exactly the same as compatible. What is the best answer? | Yes, because both are long words | *No, incompatible means not able to work together | Yes, the two words mean the same thing | No, it means very cheap
exam: Which sentence uses incompatible correctly? | «The party was incompatible, so everyone was happy and awake.» | «The two games are incompatible, so they both run perfectly on my console.» | *«The charger is incompatible with my phone, so the phone will not charge.» | «My sister bought an incompatible hat for the party.»
